Feature naming (R/clusters/markers.R and the marker stage)
--------------------------------------------------------
- marker_feature_renames in R/clusters/markers.R translates 19 ID-only
  features to gene names on the loaded object, applied in R/clusters/
  find_markers.R BEFORE FindAllMarkers (same collision-checked mechanism
  the pipeline used to make MKI67 a symbol). The marker tables and the
  feature panels therefore share gene names; the Ensembl ID stays in the
  panel comment as provenance.
- Verified against the raw BD feature list: none of the 19 target symbols
  already exists as a feature, so renames cannot collide; IDs absent from
  the object (e.g. MAL) are reported as no-ops.
- Review flags come from results/misc/Ensembl_ID/gene-mapping
  (symbol_review_required). Only CD1.1 (ENSSSCG00000025644) and IGLL1
  (ENSSSCG00000010077) are review-flagged, so only they carry the literal
  "(review)" suffix in feature names. CD163L1 and FCRL5 are NOT review-
  flagged (earlier notes here and in the SCRATCHPAD map that marked them
  for review were wrong and have been corrected).
- MKI67 is the renamed object feature from the pipeline's cell-cycle step
  (ENSSSCG00000026302 -> MKI67); the symbol is the correct feature name.
- MARCO was inspected in the original panels: present in the object but
  not returned after marker prefiltering at res 0.7. Removed from the
  current macrophage panels after the all-cluster review below.

Marker-to-publication provenance for every panel entry is recorded in
